1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Francesco_Ferdinando_d%27%C3%81valos
2 CONT
2 CONT Francesco Ferdinando d’Ávalos d'Aquino, 5th marquis of Pescara and of Vasto (c. 1530– Palermo, 1571) was commander in chief of the Spanish army in Lombardy and Piedmont, governor of the State of Milan (1560–63) and viceroy of Sici
2 CONC ly (1568–71).
2 CONT
2 CONT Francesco Ferdinando was the son of Alfonso 4th marquis of Pescara and Vasto. Still a child, he was named in 1536 Gran Camerlengo of the Kingdom of Naples. At the head of the Spanish army in Lombardy and Piedmont since december 15
2 CONC 55, he achieved an advantagious truce with France in March 1556, concluding the successful campaign started by the Duke of Alva.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was then Governor of the Duchy of Milan (1560–63) and viceroy of Sicily (1568–71), where he diminished the power of the local barons and the Deputation.
2 CONT  He also became a Knight in the Order of the Golden Fleece.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1552 he married Isabella Gonzaga, daughter of Federico II Gonzaga.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Niño aún (1536) fue nombrado gran chambelán del reino de Nápoles. En 1556, como comandante en jefe del ejército español en Lombardía y el Piamonte, consiguió una tregua en la desafortunada campaña contra los franceses iniciada por
2 CONC  el duque de Alba. Fue gobernador del Estado de Milán (1560 - 1563) y virrey de Sicilia (1568 - 1571) <p>Original: Ancora bambino (1536) fu nominato Gran Camerlengo del Regno di Napoli. Nel 1556 in qualità di comandante in capo de
2 CONC ll’esercito spagnolo in Lombardia e Piemonte, concluse con una treguala sfortunata campagna contro i francesi iniziata dal Duca d’Alba. Fu governatore dello Stato di Milano (1560 – 1563) e vicerè di Sicilia (1568 – 1571)
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
