1 NOTE His crafty and cruel character provoked civil wars from 1458 to 1462 and 
2 CONT in 1485 and alienated Pope Callistus III in 1458 and Pope Innocent VIII 
2 CONT (1432-92) from 1484 to 1492. During Ferdinand's reign the printing press 
2 CONT was introduced (1474) into Naples, and the Turks occupied (1480-81) 
2 CONT Otranto.
1 NOTE Ferrante or Ferdinand I was the natural son of Alfonso V of Aragon and Sicily.  He became heir to Naples when his father died in 1458.
1 NOTE KING OF NAPLES 1458-1494
1 NOTE (Naturale e legittimato nel 1443, da Girladona Carlino) Ferdinando I (* 2-7-1423 + Napoli 25-1-1494), Duca di  Calabria 1333/1458, Re di Napoli 1458/1494.
